---
import { MessageSquare, Users, ArrowUpRight, ShieldCheck } from '@lucide/astro';
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import { repositoryUrl, config } from '../data.mjs';
---
<Shell active="community" title="Community"><section class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">CONTINUING ENGAGEMENT</p><h1>Good Questions Make Better Systems.</h1><p>Share implementation questions, lessons learned, and feedback with the invited playbook team.</p></section><section class="community-content"><div><MessageSquare size={34} /><h2>The Playbook Conversation</h2><p>Announcements, technical examples, Q&amp;A, and lessons learned belong in this playbook's GitHub Discussions.</p>{repositoryUrl ? <a class="button" href={`${repositoryUrl}/discussions`} rel="noreferrer">Open Private Discussions<ArrowUpRight size={18} /></a> : <p class="muted">Discussions becomes available after the owner provisions this instance.</p>}<p class="access-notice"><ShieldCheck size={18} />A GitHub sign-in and accepted repository invitation are required. Viewing this website does not grant repository access.</p></div><aside><Users size={29} /><h2>Invite Your Stakeholders</h2><p>The repository owner can invite named GitHub users, check pending invitations, and revoke access through GitHub.</p>{repositoryUrl && <a class="text-link" href={`${repositoryUrl}/settings/access`} rel="noreferrer">Manage Repository Access<ArrowUpRight size={16} /></a>}<p class="access-notice">Personal-account private repositories grant collaborators write access. Read-only partner participation requires an organization-owned repository.</p><p class="muted">Revocation cannot remove material someone has already downloaded.</p></aside></section></Shell>